"Rich mages gulp potions and throw the vials away with drops still clinging inside."
"Drops from many cast-off vials of one kind can be gathered into one vial, drop by drop."
"Pill papers from mage trash hold powder whose effects range from strength to sudden sleep."
"A mage's trash pit holds more potion dregs than a mortal's; the center is where mages dump."
"Potion gunk is the chief source of impurities in ordinary trash."
"A drinker skilled in small doses can get far more from a drop than others get from a sip."
"Overusing one potion in a day blunts what each dose gives."
"A mana potion taken by an untrained body leaves a burning heat in the belly for days."
"Silver-white ash, burned past a set purity, is strongly alkaline and alchemists buy it."
"Water sprites turn a skin-melting potion into the best flesh-repair salve with a water snail."
